---
import Heading from "../../shared/ui/heading.astro";
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero__copy">
    <Heading level={1}>What is type-tune?</Heading>
    <p>type-tune moves shared TypeScript types without making you chase every import by hand.</p>
    <p>The Rust-powered CLI follows three deliberate steps:</p>
    <div class="hero__steps">
      <img src="/animation/scan-plan-apply.gif" width="1472" height="464" alt="Scan, plan, apply" />
    </div>
    <p>Review the plan first; only the moves you approve are applied.</p>
  </div>
  <img class="hero__art" src="/animation/conveyor-belt.gif" width="2400" height="1350"
    alt="A crab sorts types on a conveyor belt" fetchpriority="high" />
</section>
<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4rem;
    padding-block: 8rem 10rem;
  }
  .hero__copy {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .hero__copy p {
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0;
  }
  .hero__copy p + p {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }
  .hero__steps {
    margin-block: 1.5rem;
  }
  .hero__steps img {
    display: block;
    width: 290px;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .hero__art {
    display: block;
    width: 118.75%;
    width: round(nearest, 118.75%, 2px);
    max-width: none;
    height: auto;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-left: -4.875%;
    transform: translateY(8px);
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 2rem;
      padding-block: 0 7rem;
    }
    .hero__art {
      grid-row: 1;
      width: 123.5%;
      width: round(nearest, 123.5%, 2px);
      margin-left: -11.75%;
    }
    .hero__copy p {
      margin-top: 1rem;
    }
    .hero__steps {
      margin-block: 1.5rem 1rem;
    }
    .hero__steps img {
      width: 129px;
    }
  }
</style>
